% JWST Optical Telescope Element -- early 18-segment design ("design c").
%
% NOT the flight prescription.  This deck predates design freeze: its
% segment gap is 15 mm and its segments are 1313.25 mm flat-to-flat,
% against the flight 7 mm and 1.32 m.  Treat it as a design study.
%
% The three powered mirrors ARE the published JWST OTE prescription,
% agreeing to the published precision (McElwain et al. 2023, PASP 135,
% 058001, Table 2 -- open access, CC-BY 3.0):
%
%       here                          published
%   PM  RoC 15879.722  K -0.9966605   15,879.7  -0.9967
%   SM  RoC  1778.913  K -1.659810     1778.9   -1.6598
%   TM  RoC  3016.227  K -0.6595364    3016.2   -0.6595
%   FSM flat                           flat
%   entrance pupil 6605 mm             6.6 m
%
% Design source: TRW.
%
% The FOLD mirrors are NOT part of the published prescription.  They were
% added here, in approximate locations, to unfold the train; they carry no
% design authority and should not be cited.
%
% Element 25 is the flat FSM at a pupil -- the element the multi-zoom
% sensitivity fixture steers.  See mmacos/design/PLAN_CONFIGURATIONS.md
% section 6.  Element 27 (nElt-1) is the ExitPupil Return, which is what
% the dw_d* supervisors' reset_xp writes into.  The deck carries no
% ApStop=, so a driver must set the stop (the FSM itself is the pupil).
%
% Derived quantities of the original design, retained for reference:
%        fElt=   7.946500883D+03
%        eElt=   9.983288536D-01
%	 area = 26.68000000000000
%	 gap =  0.00500000000000
%	 areahex =  1.48222222222222
%	 f2f =  1.30825180985837
%	 p2p =  1.51063906917909
%	 P2P =  6.60459142651887d3
%	 width =  1.31325180985837d3
%        optical gap = 0.015
% SegMirMaker x=0,1,0 y=-1,0,0
% Original deck dated 9/24/03; header rewritten 2026-08-19.
%
% FIGURE CHANNELS FOR THE SENSITIVITY RUNGS (2026-08-21).  Segments 5-22
% (the 18 real segments) and the SM (elt 23) and TM (elt 24) are Surface=
% FreeForm carrying a zero-amplitude MonZernike figure channel; the SM and
% TM additionally carry a zero grid channel, both centred and sized to
% their TRACED footprint (all fields x all zoom configurations), since a
% vertex is not the beam centre and lMon is a real footprint radius.
% These are ZERO-AMPLITUDE FIXTURE CHANNELS with NO design authority --
% they exist only so the figure rungs of the configuration-axis
% sensitivity family (dw/dz MonZernike, dw/dgrid) harvest on this deck.
% The promotion from the original Surface= Conic is optically INERT (a
% zero-coefficient FreeForm computes the identical conic sag -- verified
% to <1e-10 mm, sub-picometer, against the Conic trace; gated in
% mmacos/tests/tRunSensitivities.m).  Element 4 (CenterSegment) stays
% Surface= Conic: it is a VIRTUAL element -- not a real telescope segment,
% almost entirely obscured (it passes only the chief-ray sliver, ~2.5% of
% the beam), included to pass the chief ray and serve as a PM reference --
% so its sensitivities are ~zero and it is excluded from the harvests.
% The conic base (KrElt/KcElt) and every element pose are unchanged, so
% the rigid-body (dw/dx) and prescription-parameter (dw/dsurf) rungs are
% unaffected.  Generated by
% mmacos/src/+macos/+design/promote_segments_freeform.m; see
% mmacos/design/PLAN_CONFIGURATIONS.md departure #6.

